# VibeTrack UI Patterns

Apply when editing UI files. Canonical reference: `vibetrack/src/index.css` and `vibetrack/src/App.tsx`.

## Page shell
- Root wrapper class (e.g. `.app`) with page padding and enter transition.
- Fixed `.atmosphere` layer behind content for gradients.
- Header with large `.brand` + quiet date/meta on the same baseline row.
- `main` as a single-column grid of sections.

## Section structure
```tsx
<section aria-labelledby="section-id">
  <h2 id="section-id">Title</h2>
  <p className="hint">One short supporting sentence.</p>
  {/* interaction */}
</section>
```

## Forms
- Label above control; uppercase micro-label in `--ink-soft`.
- Textarea/input share the same border, radius (~0.65rem), and focus treatment.
- Submit is an inline-flex pill with optional lucide icon (`Plus`, etc.).

## Habit / checklist rows
- Open list, not cards.
- Each row: custom checkbox + label, separated by `--line` borders.
- Hide native checkbox visually; keep it accessible; style a `.box` sibling.
- Checked: accent fill + softer label color.

## Quote block
- Display type for the quote body.
- Author as muted footer (`— Name`).
- Empty state: one quiet sentence prompting action.

## Responsive
- Below ~640px: stack header, reduce padding, stack section heads.
- Keep tap targets comfortable; preserve the same light palette.

## When extending
1. Start from CSS variables in the design-system rule.
2. Prefer new utility classes that reuse tokens over inline styles.
3. Match existing motion timing and quiet density.
4. If a border/shadow/radius can be removed without hurting understanding, remove it.
